Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.32,0:00:59.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi everyone, welcome to Munro Live.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.68,0:01:03.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've got an exciting series or episode that we're going to stitch together here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.02,0:01:08.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm with Lars, Eric, and Hector all from the Tesla team.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.33,0:01:09.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sure you know these guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.93,0:01:13.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Behind us obviously we've got the the cyber cab.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.16,0:01:15.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're going to dive into the unboxing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.97,0:01:17.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to walk a bit of the line.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.51,0:01:20.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to look at batteries, but it's going to be exciting.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.58,0:01:23.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know if it's going to be more exciting than the Roadster video from last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.55,0:01:25.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.74,0:01:30.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got to but So I mean let's let's dive into what we're seeing on the floor here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.79,0:01:33.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like what was what was the design intent?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.76,0:01:37.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like the the whole unboxing discussion came out a while ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.44,0:01:37.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,It did.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.90,0:01:41.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it we first kind of is that it was probably like five or six years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.85,0:01:45.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were working on like automating our lines more and more and more.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.04,0:01:52.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we kind of hit a wall where like the problem wasn't the automation, the problem was the design.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.74,0:01:59.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know my team is responsible for not just the design of the vehicle, not just the test of the vehicle,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.44,0:02:06.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,but also the manufacturing and even the automation groups that we have within our our team, they're all in one engineering org.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.11,0:02:09.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we got a few of us together and we're like, "How are we going to break this?"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.40,0:02:11.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And like that was the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.27,0:02:14.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,You got to break it apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.13,0:02:18.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um you know, Eric at that time was in charge of our integration team.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.42,0:02:23.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that was a big task of like 100 years of building cars one way.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.12,0:02:24.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh how do you break it apart?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.02,0:02:29.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we kind of looked at a car and realized it was a box.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.24,0:02:32.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, there's like a bottom and top, left and right, and front and back.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.92,0:02:34.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we came up with the idea to unbox it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.67,0:02:37.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And really that did two things for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.44,0:02:41.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh fundamentally, one, it gave us smaller pieces to work with.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.55,0:02:46.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we could get robots in tighter and walk through each bit um a little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.19,0:02:52.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then two, it also allowed us to break the line apart and go to more like a tributary and main flow.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.28,0:02:57.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you know, the manufacturing guys that like Hector works with, they're able to make final line.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.04,0:02:59.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many stations is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.27,0:02:59.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,25 stations?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.96,0:03:01.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,25 stations, fully automated.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.88,0:03:04.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like final GA, when the whole thing comes together is 25?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.84,0:03:05.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.32,0:03:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And like a normal Model Y was probably like 5 10X that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.44,0:03:10.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.72,0:03:12.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Depending on which factory and how much you're running.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.97,0:03:14.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, those are the two big things.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.38,0:03:16.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,But why don't we start like piece by piece?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.05,0:03:19.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Eric and I can give you a quick review and then Hector will just tell you how we put it all together.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.84,0:03:20.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.14,0:03:23.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, great. we start up front, Eric?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.84,0:03:31.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the front Yeah, the front is one of the more uh obviously dense and integrated modules that we have.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.40,0:03:32.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the business unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.48,0:03:33.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is Yeah, exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.42,0:03:38.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is basically where you know, 50%of the parts and the content really is at.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.15,0:03:39.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we did that on purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.51,0:03:45.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,We wanted to have everything isolated to one area for efficiency of low voltage distribution.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.09,0:03:50.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,We put all of the end points, all the electronics, where the control systems are.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.56,0:03:51.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, that's kind of what we've done here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.95,0:03:56.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we've also revolutionized, which we'll talk about a little bit later, how we do thermal system management,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.63,0:04:02.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,moving, you know, another step uh from our super manifold of previous products.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.07,0:04:05.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've got a 48-V low-voltage battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.32,0:04:10.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and then on top of that, we've got the drive unit, which is basically right in here in the center.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.52,0:04:15.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And one thing that we heard a lot from our service teams really early on in this project,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.84,0:04:20.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,we want to make the drive inverter serviceable without having to basically tear the car from the underside out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.04,0:04:21.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.52,0:04:25.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, what we've been able to do is allow this assembly to be very simple to remove.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.37,0:04:27.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously, washer valve is very simple to remove.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.99,0:04:35.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It allows you access to the inverter, so we don't even need to raise the car, tear the suspension, tear the drive unit out to service the inverter.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.28,0:04:40.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the fundamental aspect of integration here is is is is principally insane.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.84,0:04:41.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.40,0:04:42.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, it it really is.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.52,0:04:49.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can't like do that without thinking at the beginning, cuz Eric just very casually said, "Oh, we just take out the thermal system."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.08,0:04:50.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it's a refrigerant system, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.88,0:04:52.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't break refrigerant lines.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.20,0:04:53.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.60,0:04:55.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got rid of those. flipped it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.08,0:04:59.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a coolant-based system for heat exchange, and the refrigerant system is completely closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.52,0:05:04.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a closed-loop system within the Which you couldn't worry about after the fact, to your point.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.44,0:05:05.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you had to do it at the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.88,0:05:08.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, like, it went all the way back to the beginning of design.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.74,0:05:12.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, you know, the to to drain and purge a coolant system is actually pretty easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.64,0:05:13.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.04,0:05:18.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we even on that, we actually made a through loop, so you can push and pull and do it faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.08,0:05:18.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that's brilliant.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.84,0:05:19.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Suck it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.40,0:05:24.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,The the things that really stand out to me, I mean, we've obviously torn down a bunch of the other Teslas,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.20,0:05:28.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's it's the packaging and how tight the the drive unit is in Z.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.31,0:05:32.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, it's way higher in Z relative to the super beam.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.16,0:05:35.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And actually, you know, is So, what is mounted here?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.37,0:05:37.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is this the EAC compressor? the AC compressor.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.52,0:05:44.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, the compressor and basically the the the coolant manifold and the coolant controller are all one assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.57,0:05:46.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's all integrated together.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.08,0:05:48.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,goes back to the principle of integration and test.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.07,0:05:49.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We talked about that tributary flow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.52,0:05:52.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everything is self-tested before it goes in.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.08,0:05:54.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, when Hector's building it, he knows he has a good part.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.60,0:05:54.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.76,0:06:02.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we have a you know, a module line that builds the integrated thermal or the indirect thermal system, and that's then self-tested on the line.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.38,0:06:04.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we know we have a good part coming in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.16,0:06:06.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you'll kind of see this like every part comes together.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.52,0:06:07.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Same with the drive unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.57,0:06:13.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then by the time we get here, you have the full front end that Eric was describing with all of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.15,0:06:15.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,We actually know the car is ready to drive and go.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.39,0:06:19.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all the all of the computers are hooked up when the front end uh front comes to line.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.03,0:06:20.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it's pretty cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.88,0:06:30.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,We really took a lot of the principle of moving moving complexity out and building modules that bring assembly upstream so we can
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.55,0:06:40.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,self-test more and larger modules as well as uh in in in sub-subassemblies in a much higher percentage than anything we've ever done before.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.96,0:06:48.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other thing I I guess I'll say on the integration side, which I know you're you're keen on, is Like this has been the core team on it, seriously.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.20,0:06:50.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm keen on it as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.28,0:06:52.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, this is the core of Tesla, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.43,0:06:57.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is an organizational structure of engineering that works really well together.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.16,0:07:03.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,There is no there's no like veil, there's no wall between teams, and that's kind of what you see here. ego, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.16,0:07:04.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's no ego, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.16,0:07:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, I think Lars and I were actually, you know, talking on the ride over here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.36,0:07:12.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were talking about the patents, the designs, you know, what what is the secret sauce to Tesla?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.53,0:07:16.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think you said something like, well, it's actually not that secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.18,0:07:17.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,A lot of it's pretty public.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.46,0:07:19.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm like, I think the secret's the culture.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.59,0:07:20.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's what you just touched on.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.95,0:07:24.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's this mindset that yeah, it's not super hierarchical.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.64,0:07:25.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's our problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.68,0:07:26.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's it's it's our problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.98,0:07:31.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not your problem cuz you're the thermal guy, or you're the chassis guy, or whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.44,0:07:33.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and this is the net result.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.44,0:07:41.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And by the way, I think this is the first example that I've seen from Tesla where the EAC compressor is PIA, a part of the assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.63,0:07:43.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,No separate bracket, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.96,0:07:46.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sometimes on unintended consequences.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.40,0:07:46.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.84,0:07:50.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we actually you know, we put it all together like, oh man,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.26,0:07:58.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,this this is way more like heavier than we anticipated and we had to like re-figure out how to isolate it because it actually added to the you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.49,0:07:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the the modal mapping in the front.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.80,0:08:03.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where normally when it's sort of just a tiny little compressor, it's not that big of a deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.96,0:08:07.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's this big Well, there there's there's some like really cool stuff here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.88,0:08:12.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like are no longer running high voltage distribution from the battery pack to the system.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.81,0:08:17.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We basically do a junction off of the drive inverter to power That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.76,0:08:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.64,0:08:20.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's another Conway law break, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.72,0:08:28.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like So now the inverter team is working to make the cost of the high voltage system and the uh the thermal system less.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.71,0:08:31.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It means less parts, less complexity.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.28,0:08:34.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Uh you can ask questions that and then I'll go to the next one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.44,0:08:38.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so the inverter kind of became like this little substation for you. distribution Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.91,0:08:41.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a PDC to go and power everything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.41,0:08:44.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you're not running dedicated circuits all the way from the battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.44,0:08:46.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that is that is like 100%the core of this car.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.91,0:08:50.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is like do not waste a gram, do not waste anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.76,0:08:51.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.18,0:08:52.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.44,0:08:53.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, it's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.31,0:08:53.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.60,0:08:58.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Come around here like let's look at the suspension real quick cuz we got a lot to talk about.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.00,0:09:04.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's a it's a strut suspension which you wouldn't think with the low hood.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.70,0:09:10.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we had to offset the you know, the the kingpins to be in front of the um you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.52,0:09:17.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,the the center of the wheel there and we'll talk about this a little bit more later too, but it's also our first brake by wire system.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.40,0:09:22.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And again, that was done because it was almost a necessity for breaking it apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.64,0:09:27.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's you can't have a closed hydraulic system for breaking if you're going to split the
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.92,0:09:32.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,car in into pieces and so we can self-test the front brakes and the rear brakes separately.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.40,0:09:33.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, this is beautiful, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.46,0:09:40.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because we no longer need hydraulics running from the back to the front from a from a booster or from some kind of junction.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.96,0:09:44.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's basically everything is isolated to the module that it's in.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.92,0:09:52.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it just again allows for us to to take cost out of the distribution of whether it's conductor material or fluids or whatever it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.75,0:09:55.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It allows us to simplify manufacturing substantially.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.76,0:10:02.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so it's allowing you, if I heard what you said correctly, you're doing testing like on the thermal management system by itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.11,0:10:08.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you're able to plug all these components, brakes, drive unit, all that into the the module, this unboxed chunk,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.60,0:10:14.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then you can test it in this state to ensure before it gets bolted to the rest of the modules that this is ready to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.84,0:10:15.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.44,0:10:15.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.88,0:10:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.40,0:10:16.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.79,0:10:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're buying down risk at multiple steps, every step of the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.24,0:10:23.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, I line it What's our full percentage?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.07,0:10:23.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,85 90?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.76,0:10:25.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,They are The full line, all all of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.80,0:10:29.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's about 78%automation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.28,0:10:31.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're working on the path to to the 100.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.52,0:10:33.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,80 I'm sticking You round up just a little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.42,0:10:33.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.97,0:10:34.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.64,0:10:39.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,But to do that like you have to have super high OEE, which means all the parts going in have to be perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.88,0:10:40.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.00,0:10:41.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we test it here.
